RISC OS: decode PNG images with zlib, a row at a time.

YsPngUncompressor inflates bit by bit and hands each byte to
YsRawPngDecoder::Output, which unfilters and converts it on its own: about
160 instructions per output byte, so the 1920x990 menu picture took about
1200M instructions (around a second on a Pi) and every texture load was
slow. With YS_PNG_ZLIB (set for RISC OS in the ysbitmap CMakeLists; zlib is
in the riscos-mesa devkit):
- the IDAT data is inflated with zlib (raw deflate after the zlib header,
  so no Adler-32 pass, which the original never checked either);
- new virtual OutputBlock: YsRawPngDecoder unfilters and converts whole rows
  for non-interlaced 8-bit images of every colour type, with the same
  results as Output; other formats still go byte by byte through Output;
- Flip swaps whole rows.
tests/png-decode in riscos-ysflight decodes every runtime PNG and ~200
generated images (all colour types, sizes, tRNS, Adam7) both ways and
compares them byte for byte. Host, title00 + particle_tile + particle01 +
cloud01: about 1670M -> 330M instructions.

For ysce_public 1b13297. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

